title: Election lab
new-page: true

= Election lab

This page runs the Spanish electoral engine that the campaign will use. Votes are built from social classes, adjusted by region, and projected onto the 52 provinces. Seats are then allocated exactly as in Spain: D'Hondt in each province, a 3% threshold, and seats per province set by population.

Fed the official vote counts, the engine reproduces every Congress from 2015 to 2023. The scenarios below are illustrations of the model, not historical results.

- @lab_custom: Custom: set every party's national vote yourself
- @lab_baseline: December 2015, no change
- @lab_up_merger: Unidos Podemos and a PP recovery
- @lab_vox: Vox breaks through as Ciudadanos collapses
- @lab_landslide: A PP–Vox landslide
- @root.start_menu: Back to the main menu

@lab_baseline
on-arrival: spain_lab_scenario = 1
go-to: lab_result

@lab_up_merger
on-arrival: spain_lab_scenario = 2
go-to: lab_result

@lab_vox
on-arrival: spain_lab_scenario = 3
go-to: lab_result

@lab_landslide
on-arrival: spain_lab_scenario = 4
go-to: lab_result

@lab_result
title: Election lab result
new-page: true
on-display: {!
var keys = {1: 'baseline', 2: 'up_merger', 3: 'vox_breakthrough', 4: 'right_landslide'};
if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.SpainUI) {
    window.SpainUI.renderLab(keys[Q.spain_lab_scenario] || 'baseline');
}
!}

